# Code owners for the paths that decide what runs with release secrets.
#
# This file is half of a merge-time gate. The other half is a branch ruleset
# on `main` that requires code-owner review, with the admin role allowed to
# bypass only through a pull request. Together they replace the manual
# approval click on the `ios-code-signing` environment: a job can reach that
# environment only from `main` or an admin-created `ios-v*` tag, so whoever
# can change these paths on `main` controls what runs with the signing
# secrets.
#
# Paths not listed here have no owner and need no owner review; a pull request
# touching only android/ is not held up by this file.
#
# GitHub reads this file from the pull request's BASE branch, so editing it in
# a pull request takes effect only after that pull request merges, and the
# `/.github/` line below makes such an edit itself need owner review.
# Last matching pattern wins: never add a broader, ownerless pattern below these
# lines. tests/test_codeowners.py checks that each path stays owned.

# Every workflow (including ios-release.yml, which declares the
# ios-code-signing environment), the Apple certificates the release job pins,
# and this file.
/.github/                    @poopaskoopa

# GitHub uses the first CODEOWNERS it finds in .github/, the root, then docs/.
# Owning the other two locations means adding one needs owner review too.
/CODEOWNERS                  @poopaskoopa
/docs/CODEOWNERS             @poopaskoopa

# The iOS app, its Xcode project and test targets: compiled, tested and signed
# inside the release job.
/ios/                        @poopaskoopa

# Run on the owner's machine with privileged credentials: the iOS release
# secret uploader and distribution certificate tooling, the Azure deploy and
# budget-hook scripts, and the pre-push guardrail hook.
/scripts/                    @poopaskoopa

# Container builds published from `main` by cloud-publish.yml.
/Dockerfile*                 @poopaskoopa

# Instructions the agents follow. They run as the owner's admin account, so an
# edit here can steer an actor that is able to merge and to bypass rulesets.
/AGENTS.md                   @poopaskoopa
